WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.184
Use a low-risk goal in this fictional example: examine one practice intake draft.

00:00:05.184 --> 00:00:09.171
Clarify: what would you like to achieve when checking it?

00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:12.760
Explore: what options could help you examine the wording?

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.747
Examine: what would make each option workable within our limits?

00:00:16.747 --> 00:00:21.931
Choose: which option do you choose, or what do you need before deciding?

00:00:21.931 --> 00:00:26.317
Act: what small action will you take with the fictional draft?

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:30.703
Review: what will you check afterward to see whether it helped?

00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:34.691
Now revise the pressuring question, when will you stop resisting?

00:00:34.691 --> 00:00:41.071
Ask instead, what would you need to examine before deciding whether to try a fictional draft?

00:00:41.071 --> 00:00:45.058
The revision makes room for a concern and a choice.

00:00:45.058 --> 00:00:48.248
It leaves required approval with the accountable owner.
